  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Niger First Resilient Growth and Capital Building DPF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the First Resilient Growth and Capital-Building Development Policy Financing (DPF) for Niger is to: (1) strengthen the institutional framework for economic and social resilience to shocks; (2) improve service delivery to build physical and human capital; and (3) enhance governance over natural resources. The DPF supports the goals on developing human capital, improving public access to services, and on structural transformation in the government&apos;s third economic and social development plan 2022-2026. It also supports Niger&apos;s intended nationally determined contribution&apos;s goal of a low-carbon development path and building a more climate resilient economy, including through the strengthening of the disaster risk management (DRM) framework and social protection system, promotion of renewable energy sources and management of water resources.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of this DPO is to  (1) strengthen the institutional framework for  economic and social resilience to shocks; (2) improve service delivery to build physical and human capital; and (3) enhance governance over natural resources.</narrative>
